WEBVTT

00:00:05.714 --> 00:00:06.757
Was I mean to you?

00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:08.716
That would've required
you to speak to me.

00:00:08.883 --> 00:00:10.134
Lot's changed in a year, huh?

00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:12.719
- Are we really gonna do this?
- I think we already are.

00:00:13.052 --> 00:00:15.887
- He really loves me, Ryan.
- You ran away to get away from him.

00:00:16.054 --> 00:00:18.306
- Then you took off without calling?
- Like when you left Chino.

00:00:18.472 --> 00:00:20.891
- How'd it go with the liquor board?
- Working on it.

00:00:21.057 --> 00:00:23.517
As of today,
I'm the only chance your father has.

00:00:23.726 --> 00:00:26.186
You wouldn't want my mom to know
you blackmailed me into living with her?

00:00:26.519 --> 00:00:28.979
You know what we haven't done
in a while?

00:00:36.233 --> 00:00:37.818
- Two weeks.
- Sorry?

00:00:38.026 --> 00:00:41.028
Two weeks. Unbelievable.

00:00:41.195 --> 00:00:42.612
Who would believe it? I don't.

00:00:42.779 --> 00:00:46.532
It's the Tourette's flaring up again.
Happens now and again, but it's fine.

00:00:46.698 --> 00:00:49.367
Julie and Caleb's wedding invitation.
Getting married in...

00:00:49.533 --> 00:00:51.868
- Two weeks.
- Wow, they're really doing it.

00:00:52.035 --> 00:00:54.286
An unfortunate image just leapt
in my mind.

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:56.955
I mean, I don't understand.
What is the rush?

00:00:57.122 --> 00:00:59.290
It's the gruesome twosome.
What do you expect?

00:00:59.456 --> 00:01:01.499
It's the shock-and-awe approach
to courtship.

00:01:01.916 --> 00:01:05.627
Julie Cooper's getting married
to my father and you're being flip.

00:01:05.794 --> 00:01:07.586
Me, being flip about Caleb?

00:01:07.753 --> 00:01:11.672
No. I'm kind of softening on the guy.
He may not be friendly or ethical...

00:01:11.839 --> 00:01:14.007
...or, you know, a million laughs.
- But he is...

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:17.593
Generous. Well, either that
or he's in love and delusional...

00:01:17.759 --> 00:01:19.886
...because he threw out
a ballpark figure...

00:01:20.053 --> 00:01:22.888
...for what he's offering Jimmy and me
for the restaurant...

00:01:23.054 --> 00:01:25.848
...it ain't chump change.
- So he's bought your acceptance.

00:01:26.015 --> 00:01:27.599
But at a very high price.

00:01:27.766 --> 00:01:30.309
Hey, how's Marissa dealing
with her new stepdad?

00:01:30.893 --> 00:01:32.685
Yeah, is she all right with all that?

00:01:32.894 --> 00:01:35.646
- She's in the wedding. She agreed to that.
- And you two?

00:01:35.812 --> 00:01:38.356
You...
What, are you back to...?

00:01:38.647 --> 00:01:40.190
Yeah, yeah, we're good, actually.

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:41.774
Really good.

00:01:41.983 --> 00:01:44.610
Really good for you is like singing
from the treetops.

00:01:44.818 --> 00:01:48.153
Now that you and Marissa are good,
does that mean you and Theresa are over?

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.321
Yeah, yeah.
Me and Theresa, yeah.

00:01:50.488 --> 00:01:53.282
Well, now that we've got your
love life straightened out...

00:01:53.448 --> 00:01:55.950
...I think it might be time to take
a step back...

00:01:56.117 --> 00:01:58.702
...and untangle this incestuous web
I like to call...

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:01.203
...the "Julie-Caleb union."
Let's think about this.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:05.122
When this bizarro knot gets tied, Julie
Cooper's gonna be your mother-in-law.

00:02:06.915 --> 00:02:08.833
Yeah, enjoy.
She's gonna be your stepmom.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.292
Seth, my head is spinning.

00:02:10.459 --> 00:02:12.710
Yeah. Yeah.
Me and Marissa, we could be related.

00:02:12.877 --> 00:02:14.170
I can't even do that math.

00:02:14.336 --> 00:02:17.839
But the real kicker is:
Julie Cooper, my grandma.

00:02:18.798 --> 00:02:20.882
My grandma wears Uggs.
Think about it.

00:02:21.049 --> 00:02:22.925
I am thinking about it.

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:24.718
- Hello.
- Hi.

00:02:24.885 --> 00:02:26.636
It's Theresa, Ryan's friend.

00:02:26.803 --> 00:02:29.262
Oh, hey there. How are you?
Let me get him for you.

00:02:29.471 --> 00:02:31.681
Actually, I'm calling for you.

00:02:32.264 --> 00:02:34.724
I was wondering if maybe we could meet.

00:02:35.099 --> 00:02:39.811
- Are you all right?
- I just have a legal question.

00:02:39.977 --> 00:02:42.271
- Can we meet?
- Sure, you name the spot.

00:02:42.479 --> 00:02:44.939
I picked up some catering shifts
at the Balboa Bakery.

00:02:45.147 --> 00:02:47.274
I have a break at 1
if you want to stop by.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.775
- And, Mr. Cohen, one more thing.
- Yeah.

00:02:50.484 --> 00:02:52.944
Please don't say anything to Ryan
about any of this.

00:02:54.945 --> 00:02:56.363
You got it.

00:02:56.529 --> 00:02:58.281
I'll see you then.

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:50.186
- Hello.
- I need one minute.

00:03:50.352 --> 00:03:52.812
You and me both.
You have no idea how hard it is...

00:03:49.977 --> 00:03:52.312
...to plan a spectacular wedding
in only two weeks.

00:03:52.479 --> 00:03:54.188
Mr. Lasser, could you repeat that?

00:03:54.355 --> 00:03:56.523
I have a caterer
who refuses to serve beef.

00:04:00.692 --> 00:04:03.110
Something about a mad cow
wiping out Newport Beach?

00:03:59.275 --> 00:04:01.693
- Julie, phone.
- Ironically, the minister I wanted...

00:04:01.859 --> 00:04:05.528
...is away on his honeymoon. My wedding
planner's a passive-aggressive nitwit...

00:04:05.695 --> 00:04:08.197
...who has the audacity to question
my taste in music.

00:04:08.364 --> 00:04:10.907
Bob Seger is not "so over."

00:04:11.074 --> 00:04:14.075
I'm going to have to call you back.

00:04:14.576 --> 00:04:17.202
- How can I help?
- Normally, I would never bother you.

00:04:17.369 --> 00:04:20.163
But there is one small thing
you can help me with: A shower.

00:04:20.329 --> 00:04:24.040
- And by "help," I mean "host."
- Julie, I can't host a shower.

00:04:31.253 --> 00:04:34.755
I know it's last-minute, but I thought
as my maid of honor, you'd want to.

00:04:27.917 --> 00:04:29.502
Wait.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:31.003
Your maid of honor?

00:04:31.169 --> 00:04:33.504
You're my closest friend.
Who else would it be?

00:04:33.671 --> 00:04:35.089
Well, I was thinking Marissa.

00:04:35.797 --> 00:04:37.674
I'm not Marissa's
favorite person right now.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.426
Caleb's convinced he can get her to help,
and he's made all the arrangements...

00:04:41.593 --> 00:04:43.052
...to have it at the club.

00:04:43.219 --> 00:04:45.178
- In that case...
- You're a godsend!

00:04:45.387 --> 00:04:49.264
Thank you. And one more thing: Let's not
have one of those tacky, girly showers...

00:04:49.473 --> 00:04:52.433
...with games about making whoopee.
- Don't say "whoopee."

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.852
I was thinking a couples shower, elegant.
A cocktail party with gifts.

00:04:56.018 --> 00:04:58.979
What do you think?
Any other questions, just ask Marissa.

00:04:59.312 --> 00:05:00.896
Thanks.

00:05:07.942 --> 00:05:09.694
A couples shower?

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:12.987
- What is a couples shower?
- Something I'm not throwing for my mom.

00:05:13.154 --> 00:05:16.281
That was a message from Caleb
saying that per our arrangement...

00:05:16.448 --> 00:05:18.699
...he wants me to help Kirsten
throw a shower for my mom.

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:22.285
What about moving in with them?
Have you told your dad yet?

00:05:23.369 --> 00:05:25.704
No, but I will.

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:29.164
- Today.
- Lf you don't want to throw this shower...

00:05:29.331 --> 00:05:33.125
...then don't. Stand your ground.
- Standing my ground isn't my strong suit.

00:05:33.417 --> 00:05:35.501
- That's true.
- Pac-Man. Rematch?

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:39.004
Hey, I almost, maybe,
might beat you this time.

00:05:42.923 --> 00:05:44.549
What is it with those two?

00:05:44.715 --> 00:05:47.634
The Pac-Man and the getting along
and the happy times.

00:05:47.842 --> 00:05:50.511
They're playing video games.
It's not a Mandy Moore movie.

00:05:50.719 --> 00:05:53.554
She's supposed to be crying
and he's supposed to be brooding.

00:05:53.763 --> 00:05:56.139
- That's how it works.
- Hello?

00:05:56.306 --> 00:05:59.767
Hi. Yeah, we're still on for tonight.

00:06:00.058 --> 00:06:02.060
Fajitas? Yeah, okay.

00:06:02.226 --> 00:06:03.561
I'm gonna make the margs.

00:06:03.727 --> 00:06:06.020
Kidding. God. Oh, my God, I know.

00:06:06.187 --> 00:06:08.272
Oh, my God. No, you're so funny.

00:06:08.439 --> 00:06:11.065
No, you are. No, you.

00:06:11.232 --> 00:06:12.733
Okay, I'll see you later.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:14.442
Bye, Dad.

00:06:15.109 --> 00:06:17.444
Dad? That's how you talk to your dad?

00:06:17.653 --> 00:06:21.405
- How's how I talk to my dad?
- Like he's your friend.

00:06:21.572 --> 00:06:24.240
- He is. He's my best friend.
- Why have I never met him?

00:06:24.407 --> 00:06:26.033
I was wondering if you had parents.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.701
I thought you were made
in a lab or hatched in a pod.

00:06:28.868 --> 00:06:30.703
We haven't done
a family meet-and-greet.

00:06:30.869 --> 00:06:34.455
I know we haven't which is odd,
considering that you've met my dad...

00:06:34.622 --> 00:06:37.290
...you've met my mom, Captain Oats,
the list goes on.

00:06:37.457 --> 00:06:39.833
I've never introduced a boyfriend
to my dad before.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.334
It's kind of a big deal.

00:06:42.043 --> 00:06:44.586
Well, you're forgetting
one key factor here, Summer.

00:06:44.795 --> 00:06:46.045
Parents love me, okay?

00:06:46.254 --> 00:06:49.172
I've got this non-threatening,
non-sexual vibe they eat up.

00:06:49.339 --> 00:06:52.174
We'll go miniature golfing or hot-tubbing
or something fun.

00:06:52.383 --> 00:06:54.467
Well, my stepmom's at Canyon Ranch.

00:06:54.676 --> 00:06:57.761
- Drying out?
- No, some stress-management program.

00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:00.138
She has anxiety issues.

00:07:00.471 --> 00:07:01.889
So?

00:07:02.514 --> 00:07:04.432
- We can go to lunch with my dad.
- Nice.

00:07:04.599 --> 00:07:06.850
You sure you want to skip the hot tub?

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:08.601
Okay, lunch is good.

00:07:08.768 --> 00:07:11.770
We'll do lunch. But your dad's
not going to need a menu...

00:07:11.937 --> 00:07:15.522
...because he's gonna be eating
out of the palm of my hand.

00:07:18.149 --> 00:07:20.817
The palm of my hand, Summer.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.779
Hey.

00:07:27.655 --> 00:07:29.823
Oh, my God.

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:33.659
- Who did that to you?
- Sorry to call you out of the blue like this.

00:07:33.825 --> 00:07:37.995
- Was it Eddie?
- He's been under a lot of stress.

00:07:38.412 --> 00:07:41.705
He lost his job and his apartment.

00:07:43.456 --> 00:07:46.375
The other night,
he had a couple drinks, and he just...

00:07:46.583 --> 00:07:48.876
...went off.
- So you're leaving him, I hope.

00:07:51.837 --> 00:07:53.046
It's complicated.

00:07:53.921 --> 00:07:55.297
I know, it should be simple.

00:07:55.506 --> 00:07:57.882
Your boyfriend hits you,
you leave him, right?

00:07:58.632 --> 00:08:00.425
It's never simple.

00:08:00.759 --> 00:08:02.385
How can I help you?

00:08:02.593 --> 00:08:04.428
I just need to know, you know...

00:08:04.595 --> 00:08:07.972
...if he does this again, what would
happen to him if I pressed charges?

00:08:08.138 --> 00:08:11.307
It depends, anything from
a restraining order to jail time.

00:08:12.266 --> 00:08:14.726
You're not still thinking
about marrying the guy?

00:08:14.934 --> 00:08:18.061
Not if you gotta ask
these kinds of questions.

00:08:25.232 --> 00:08:28.234
So, you, me, my dad,
lunch tomorrow at the club.

00:08:28.401 --> 00:08:32.028
Awesome. By the end of this lunch,
I predict your father and I...

00:08:32.195 --> 00:08:35.280
...smoking Cuban cigars. Know
what I'm saying? Trading Viagra yuks.

00:08:35.447 --> 00:08:37.740
Maybe I'll put on a little Dean Martin.
I don't know.

00:08:37.907 --> 00:08:40.075
- You know he's not 75, right?
- I do know that...

00:08:40.242 --> 00:08:42.410
...but male bonding's a very
old-school activity.

00:08:42.577 --> 00:08:44.328
We may not make it through lunch.

00:08:44.494 --> 00:08:46.704
We may skip straight
over to the Russian baths.

00:08:46.871 --> 00:08:50.165
- Okay, tomorrow just sit under a light.
- What?

00:08:50.331 --> 00:08:52.458
Sit under a light.
He wants to see you better.

00:08:52.708 --> 00:08:54.834
Order steak.
He thinks greens are effeminate.

00:08:55.043 --> 00:08:57.544
Celery's gay, got it.
What else you got? I want to prep...

00:08:57.753 --> 00:09:00.588
...make sure I lock into
some witty anecdotes, my A material.

00:09:00.796 --> 00:09:03.548
- He's a plastic surgeon.
- I know what he does for a living...

00:09:03.757 --> 00:09:06.758
...and we can have fun with that,
but let's talk about hobbies.

00:09:06.925 --> 00:09:08.509
What do you guys talk about?

00:09:09.177 --> 00:09:10.511
Mostly we talk about me.

00:09:10.969 --> 00:09:13.221
- You?
- Yeah, it's like our common interest.

00:09:15.347 --> 00:09:17.307
- You wanted to meet him.
- I do. I do.

00:09:17.473 --> 00:09:20.434
I just was kind of hoping for some...
You know what I mean?

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:22.018
Look...

00:09:22.852 --> 00:09:25.020
...my dad really loves me.

00:09:25.187 --> 00:09:27.146
And I really like you.

00:09:27.313 --> 00:09:30.231
So he's gonna really like you.

00:09:30.648 --> 00:09:33.192
- Right?
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:09:33.692 --> 00:09:35.193
Yeah.

00:09:44.449 --> 00:09:46.116
We should go to the bedroom.

00:09:46.283 --> 00:09:47.867
Yeah.

00:09:50.119 --> 00:09:52.412
Oh, but Marissa,
she's gonna be home soon.

00:09:52.579 --> 00:09:56.248
- Right, right, right. We should...
- Yeah.

00:09:56.456 --> 00:09:59.416
I'm sorry. I'm sorry about all this
sneaking around.

00:09:59.625 --> 00:10:01.834
It's so incredibly high-school.

00:10:04.628 --> 00:10:06.171
Dad. Hailey?

00:10:06.838 --> 00:10:08.630
Hey, kiddo. Hi.

00:10:09.339 --> 00:10:11.924
Hailey was just over to help me fix my...

00:10:12.091 --> 00:10:14.217
- Faucet.
- My faucet, which is...

00:10:14.384 --> 00:10:19.554
Remember it was leaking? And, you know,
she's an expert on plumbing.

00:10:21.055 --> 00:10:22.389
- I should go.
- Okay.

00:10:22.556 --> 00:10:24.974
Now that the faucet is, you know, fixed.

00:10:25.141 --> 00:10:26.892
Okay. Listen, thank you so much.

00:10:27.059 --> 00:10:30.227
You know, if anything else breaks
then I'll give you a call.

00:10:30.394 --> 00:10:31.895
But thank you.

00:10:32.062 --> 00:10:33.646
- Bye.
- See you.

00:10:36.023 --> 00:10:38.816
Wow. You guys really need to work
on your improv skills.

00:10:38.983 --> 00:10:41.609
Look, I wanted to talk to you about it.
I did, but l...

00:10:41.776 --> 00:10:46.237
With your mom and Caleb, the last thing
you needed to deal with was this.

00:10:46.404 --> 00:10:49.114
Dad, I'm fine with it.

00:10:49.281 --> 00:10:53.492
You know what? Better than that,
I'm happy for you.

00:10:58.453 --> 00:11:00.121
What's the matter?

00:11:02.039 --> 00:11:05.458
It's just with Mom and Caleb
getting married...

00:11:05.624 --> 00:11:07.375
...and they're moving
into this new house...

00:11:07.584 --> 00:11:12.795
I know a lot is changing, kiddo,
but it's not all bad.

00:11:13.004 --> 00:11:15.255
- You know Caleb is buying the restaurant?
- I know.

00:11:15.422 --> 00:11:17.507
Yeah. And, you know,
we're gonna be okay.

00:11:17.674 --> 00:11:20.008
I mean, like, seriously okay.

00:11:20.175 --> 00:11:22.802
We're talking millions of dollars.

00:11:22.969 --> 00:11:27.388
We're gonna get out of this place,
move into a real home and start over.

00:11:29.514 --> 00:11:30.723
Isn't that great?

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:33.725
Yeah. Yeah, it's great.

00:11:38.437 --> 00:11:41.105
- Seth's meeting your dad?
- Yeah, so?

00:11:41.272 --> 00:11:43.356
Well, that's gonna go well.

00:11:43.523 --> 00:11:46.567
Well, actually, Marissa,
it will go well. Do you know why?

00:11:46.733 --> 00:11:48.401
Turns out I'm great
with the parents.

00:11:48.568 --> 00:11:51.403
- I'm better with parents than daughters.
- I believe that.

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:54.863
I think we know I'm pretty good
with the daughters. Know what I mean?

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:57.782
This little one right here.
Her daddy's gonna feel it.

00:11:57.949 --> 00:12:00.492
- Yeah.
- I can't believe Eddie would hit her.

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:05.162
I know. And Theresa has made it clear
she does not want to press charges.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:08.372
So unless she changes her mind,
there's only so much I can do.

00:12:08.539 --> 00:12:10.707
At least you gave her someone
to talk to...

00:12:10.915 --> 00:12:13.041
...somewhere to go. It's a start.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:16.710
Yeah, until she decides to go back
to Chino and marry the guy anyway.

00:12:16.877 --> 00:12:19.879
What about Ryan?
He must be beside himself.

00:12:20.046 --> 00:12:22.089
You wouldn't know it
from looking at him.

00:12:22.256 --> 00:12:23.757
- He doesn't know.
- What?

00:12:23.923 --> 00:12:26.175
Theresa had me promise
that I wouldn't tell him.

00:12:26.341 --> 00:12:29.385
She knows he'd fly off the handle.

00:12:29.552 --> 00:12:32.178
He'd go back to Chino
and beat the daylights out of Eddie.

00:12:32.345 --> 00:12:34.888
He breaks his probation
and he ends up back in juvie.

00:12:36.723 --> 00:12:39.350
Ryan, need something?
More soda?

00:12:39.516 --> 00:12:41.893
I got it. What's going on?

00:12:42.435 --> 00:12:44.269
Nothing.

00:12:45.729 --> 00:12:47.230
Nothing.

00:12:47.438 --> 00:12:49.356
Nothing. Okay.

00:12:58.778 --> 00:13:01.280
Come on, just pick one.
Marissa's gonna be here soon.

00:13:01.447 --> 00:13:03.490
Don't rush me.
I've got a lot riding on this.

00:13:03.656 --> 00:13:05.699
You said you were great with parents.

00:13:05.866 --> 00:13:09.785
Yeah, I've got so much experience being
introduced to my girlfriend's parents.

00:13:09.994 --> 00:13:11.787
Damn it, I'm being sarcastic.

00:13:11.953 --> 00:13:13.913
So? Sarcasm's like breathing for you.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:15.914
Her dad thinks it's a sign of weakness.

00:13:16.123 --> 00:13:18.582
- Sounds like a smart man.
- I have to fool him.

00:13:18.833 --> 00:13:21.960
Do you understand?
I have to spin an elaborate web of lies...

00:13:22.126 --> 00:13:24.545
...smoke and mirrors, for an entire meal.

00:13:24.711 --> 00:13:26.671
Only then can I earn his trust.

00:13:27.088 --> 00:13:30.048
- I hope you're not like this during lunch.
- This one? Too edgy?

00:13:30.215 --> 00:13:32.174
- Too fashion-forward?
- It's a white shirt.

00:13:32.341 --> 00:13:35.260
That's a good point.
White shirts make my teeth look yellow.

00:13:35.426 --> 00:13:39.012
That's Marissa. I've gotta go find her
before she runs into her mom.

00:13:46.934 --> 00:13:50.519
- Hey.
- Hey. Your mom's in there with Kirsten.

00:13:50.686 --> 00:13:55.272
- Maybe I'll come back later.
- No, you told Kirsten you'd stop by, right?

00:13:56.106 --> 00:13:59.483
I don't want to deal with my mom now.
All I want is to get back at her...

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:03.486
...and here I am throwing her a party.
- It'll be fine. Just take the high road.

00:14:03.652 --> 00:14:05.362
- You can't lose.
- This looks great...

00:14:05.528 --> 00:14:08.322
...fruited Israeli couscous.

00:14:09.322 --> 00:14:12.158
- Oh, honey, hi.
- Hey.

00:14:12.324 --> 00:14:13.617
Thanks for coming.

00:14:13.825 --> 00:14:15.952
So you stopped by to help us, huh?

00:14:16.118 --> 00:14:20.163
Actually, Kirsten called me,
so I stopped by to help Kirsten.

00:14:21.122 --> 00:14:23.832
Well, then I'll let you get to it.

00:14:23.998 --> 00:14:26.000
- Kirsten. Ryan.
- Julie.

00:14:27.792 --> 00:14:29.919
- You okay?
- Fine.

00:14:30.085 --> 00:14:31.670
So, what can I do to help?

00:14:32.087 --> 00:14:34.380
Double check the guest list
with the invitations.

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:37.965
I have everyone from The Newport Group,
all the ladies from spin class.

00:14:38.132 --> 00:14:42.718
- But there's no one from Julie's family.
- My mom and her parents don't speak.

00:14:42.885 --> 00:14:44.303
What about her sisters?

00:14:44.469 --> 00:14:46.262
Well, there's always Aunt Cindy.

00:14:48.347 --> 00:14:49.973
The caterers. Great.

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:52.641
Aunt Cindy, you'll get in touch with her?

00:14:52.808 --> 00:14:54.351
Yeah.

00:14:56.602 --> 00:14:58.937
See? Take the high road.

00:14:59.104 --> 00:15:01.563
You've never met Aunt Cindy.

00:15:08.109 --> 00:15:09.443
Well.

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:13.654
- It's... It's...
- It's more than twice what we put into it.

00:15:13.821 --> 00:15:16.990
Caught me at a good time. A man
in love has no right doing business.

00:15:17.157 --> 00:15:19.658
- Besides, we're family.
- Right. Are we? I don't know.

00:15:19.867 --> 00:15:21.993
- I can't keep track.
- Now, if you'll excuse me...

00:15:22.201 --> 00:15:25.078
...my fianc Áe wants help picking out
linens for the reception.

00:15:25.245 --> 00:15:27.830
I had no idea there were so many
shades of beige.

00:15:29.748 --> 00:15:31.916
All right, we'll see you.

00:15:33.917 --> 00:15:35.168
He's up to something.

00:15:35.335 --> 00:15:38.378
Either that or he's on some
serious painkillers.

00:15:38.545 --> 00:15:41.839
But you know what? I don't care.
Two and a half million dollars?

00:15:43.548 --> 00:15:45.174
I can finally breathe again.

00:15:45.341 --> 00:15:47.467
I'm happy for you.

00:15:48.218 --> 00:15:49.427
- But?
- Well...

00:15:49.593 --> 00:15:52.470
...I wish it could have been the place
that did it, not Caleb.

00:15:52.637 --> 00:15:56.264
I thought we'd be rescued by meat loaf
and dirty martinis.

00:15:56.431 --> 00:15:58.099
That's how it was supposed to be.

00:15:58.266 --> 00:16:01.559
Think about it. All that meat loaf
you'd be making? It's off your hands.

00:16:01.726 --> 00:16:03.102
Now you've got time for work.

00:16:03.352 --> 00:16:05.353
That's what I was trying
to get away from.

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:06.813
No, no. I mean real work.

00:16:06.979 --> 00:16:08.647
The stuff that you love.

00:16:08.814 --> 00:16:11.107
Like rescuing kids...

00:16:11.274 --> 00:16:15.109
...and down-and-out guys who are
millions of dollars in debt.

00:16:15.276 --> 00:16:18.945
Come on, right now there's a stray
out there just waiting for you...

00:16:19.154 --> 00:16:22.239
...to swoop down and save the day.

00:16:23.365 --> 00:16:27.617
Remember, we are off-our-asses wasted
and totally lost in the woods...

00:16:27.826 --> 00:16:32.078
...and I gotta go like nobody's business,
so I end up dropping trou right there.

00:16:32.245 --> 00:16:34.747
Sure enough, poison oak everywhere.

00:16:34.913 --> 00:16:37.082
Julie tells the whole school.

00:16:37.248 --> 00:16:38.916
What a bitch, right?

00:16:39.124 --> 00:16:41.793
- Charming story.
- Yeah, good times.

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:43.627
Mind if I smoke?

00:16:43.794 --> 00:16:46.254
- Actually, l...
- Sorry.

00:16:46.629 --> 00:16:49.798
I tried to quit once,
but I ended up putting on 30 pounds.

00:16:49.965 --> 00:16:52.466
And who wants to have sex
with that, right?

00:16:55.176 --> 00:16:58.845
Aunt Cindy. Look at you!

00:16:59.012 --> 00:17:01.222
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:17:01.388 --> 00:17:03.265
- So this is my boyfriend, Ryan.
- Hi.

00:17:03.431 --> 00:17:06.642
Cindy's been telling me some priceless
stories about your mom.

00:17:07.309 --> 00:17:10.019
Yeah, I was telling her about Julie's
Def Leppard phase.

00:17:10.186 --> 00:17:14.355
- She drove us to Anaheim to scalp tickets.
- I can't believe she was into heavy metal.

00:17:14.522 --> 00:17:18.649
- I can't believe she ever went to Anaheim.
- So where is the belle of the ball anyway?

00:17:18.816 --> 00:17:21.109
Doing yoga? Getting Botox?

00:17:21.859 --> 00:17:24.153
You and Julie, do you talk often?

00:17:24.361 --> 00:17:27.863
Sure, if you call once every
seven years often.

00:17:29.114 --> 00:17:32.658
Look, I'll hand it to you straight.
I was shocked she wanted me here.

00:17:32.825 --> 00:17:34.242
- You were?
- Yeah.

00:17:34.409 --> 00:17:38.620
Last time I saw her, and memory's a little
foggy on account of the Jell-O shots...

00:17:38.787 --> 00:17:42.164
...I'm pretty sure she told me to get lost,
for good.

00:17:44.248 --> 00:17:46.083
Marissa, can I talk to you in...?

00:17:46.625 --> 00:17:50.711
Oh, hi. I'm so sorry,
I don't mean to interrupt, but...

00:17:54.296 --> 00:17:58.841
- What the hell are you doing here?
- Well, it's nice to see you too.

00:17:59.008 --> 00:18:02.260
I'm here because I was invited
by Marissa.

00:18:04.845 --> 00:18:08.806
- Marissa, is this true?
- You guys have tons to catch up on...

00:18:08.972 --> 00:18:12.683
...so I'll give you some alone time.
- We should probably get that cake too.

00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:15.226
Right. Have fun.

00:18:22.314 --> 00:18:25.733
And I decided that I wanted to celebrate
both holidays, so what I did...

00:18:25.941 --> 00:18:28.860
...is, basically, I combined them,
and I made Chrismukkah.

00:18:30.736 --> 00:18:32.529
Like Christmas and Hanukkah.

00:18:32.737 --> 00:18:34.196
- Chrismukkah.
- Chrismukkah.

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:37.532
Chrismukkah.
Well, that must be a lot of fun for you.

00:18:37.699 --> 00:18:41.326
Yeah, we have fun with it. But I don't
want you to think I'm all about...

00:18:41.493 --> 00:18:44.328
...holiday cheer,
I'm hoarding all of them or anything.

00:18:44.494 --> 00:18:46.204
I have interests. I have hobbies.

00:18:46.371 --> 00:18:47.663
- Do you?
- Sure, I do, sir.

00:18:47.997 --> 00:18:50.290
- Comic books, for one.
- Comic books.

00:18:50.707 --> 00:18:53.959
Sir, I think I hear the skepticism
in your tone.

00:18:54.125 --> 00:18:56.585
And I understand,
but I just want to tell you...

00:18:56.752 --> 00:19:00.755
...I believe the comic book is a legitimate
art form. Frank Miller's Sin City...

00:19:00.921 --> 00:19:02.172
...Powers by Brian Bendis...

00:19:02.297 --> 00:19:04.799
...arguably one of the best writers
in comics today.

00:19:04.966 --> 00:19:08.885
I mean, combines sort of the storytelling
panache of, like, a Stan Lee...

00:19:09.051 --> 00:19:11.845
...that old-school vibe,
but mixed with a lyrical...

00:19:12.012 --> 00:19:14.888
...you know, sophistication of...
I want to say Alan Moore.

00:19:15.055 --> 00:19:19.058
It's probably too inside for you. You're
probably a fan of the classics. Superman?

00:19:19.850 --> 00:19:22.518
Batman fan? No?

00:19:23.852 --> 00:19:25.562
Iceman?

00:19:26.396 --> 00:19:28.856
He freezes things.

00:19:29.981 --> 00:19:31.857
- So, Summer...
- Isn't Summer the best?

00:19:32.066 --> 00:19:35.151
Little force of nature, just sitting there.
Little live wire.

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:38.403
- Yes, she is.
- I think she's so full of vim and vigor.

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:41.155
What, in your surgical opinion,
does she have more of?

00:19:41.322 --> 00:19:43.573
Would you say it's vim or vigor?

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:46.408
- Cohen, what are you talking about?
- Summer. Summer...

00:19:46.575 --> 00:19:50.619
...I'm just saying that I think you've been
extraordinarily blessed with vim.

00:19:50.786 --> 00:19:53.538
- And vigor too, sir.
- What do you say we order?

00:19:53.704 --> 00:19:55.205
Okay. I like food.

00:19:55.372 --> 00:19:56.915
Yes.

00:20:02.752 --> 00:20:05.420
So we just say that we're very
happy together.

00:20:05.587 --> 00:20:08.088
- We hope that they can be happy for us.
- Yeah.

00:20:08.255 --> 00:20:10.381
- You know?
- Easy.

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:14.801
Hailey?

00:20:14.968 --> 00:20:16.469
The door?

00:20:16.969 --> 00:20:18.970
What if it isn't the right time...

00:20:19.137 --> 00:20:22.973
...because my dad's getting married to
Julie. And Kirsten's planning the shower...

00:20:23.139 --> 00:20:25.683
You know what? We should wait
until the timing's right.

00:20:25.849 --> 00:20:27.726
Know what I'm saying?
The timing's wrong.

00:20:27.892 --> 00:20:29.310
- Yeah.
- Right. Okay, good.

00:20:29.477 --> 00:20:31.103
- Okay, great.
- Excellent.

00:20:31.311 --> 00:20:32.770
This is a good idea too.

00:20:32.979 --> 00:20:34.939
- I'm so sorry.
- I feel so...

00:20:38.566 --> 00:20:40.609
Did you see the look on my mom's face?

00:20:40.817 --> 00:20:44.111
- So much for the high road.
- Yeah, this is way more fun.

00:20:44.528 --> 00:20:47.196
Hi, we're here to pick up
a cake for Cooper.

00:20:47.363 --> 00:20:49.448
- Let me check on that.
- Thanks.

00:20:54.034 --> 00:20:57.161
Oh, my God, this is amazing.
You've got to try this.

00:21:00.746 --> 00:21:02.831
- You need another piece.
- Stop!

00:21:09.001 --> 00:21:10.502
Theresa, what happened?

00:21:13.004 --> 00:21:14.672
- Eddie?
- I didn't want you involved.

00:21:14.838 --> 00:21:19.341
You weren't supposed to know I was
here. I guess Sandy told you anyway.

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:22.385
Sandy...
Sandy knows about this?

00:21:32.224 --> 00:21:34.100
Hey, where have you been?

00:21:34.267 --> 00:21:36.936
I couldn't sleep.
I thought watching the sun come up...

00:21:37.144 --> 00:21:39.979
...and getting my ass kicked
by some 4-footers would help.

00:21:40.146 --> 00:21:41.147
It didn't.

00:21:41.355 --> 00:21:45.358
Here's that vanilla half-caf caramel
macchiato on the dry side you love.

00:21:45.524 --> 00:21:48.901
It's so good.
It's only 1500 calories per sip.

00:21:49.068 --> 00:21:52.237
- Hey, what time is that shower today?
- Why?

00:21:52.404 --> 00:21:56.406
- I might be late, depending on traffic.
- We live 10 minutes from the club.

00:21:56.573 --> 00:21:58.449
- I'll be coming from Chino.
- What?

00:21:58.699 --> 00:22:01.326
I want to pay Eddie a visit,
knock some sense into him.

00:22:02.118 --> 00:22:05.662
Metaphorically, of course.
At the very least, give him a good scare.

00:22:06.371 --> 00:22:09.414
- I'm taking back the coffee.
- People here need to hear from you.

00:22:09.581 --> 00:22:13.041
- Ryan is really upset.
- What can I do?

00:22:13.208 --> 00:22:15.460
- He won't talk to me.
- Explain it to him...

00:22:15.626 --> 00:22:18.753
...instead of trying to match him glare
for glare. What about Theresa?

00:22:19.087 --> 00:22:21.922
The victim, alone, in the motel room.

00:22:22.172 --> 00:22:24.132
She'd love to hear from you.

00:22:24.299 --> 00:22:26.758
Why don't you call her and invite her over.

00:22:26.925 --> 00:22:29.468
- You can keep the coffee.
- Thank you.

00:22:36.723 --> 00:22:39.725
I know you're pissed off.
I would have explained things to you...

00:22:39.933 --> 00:22:42.185
...but I couldn't
until Theresa gave me the okay.

00:22:42.393 --> 00:22:44.269
You guys decided to include me.
Thanks.

00:22:44.478 --> 00:22:46.896
I'm a lawyer. She asked for privacy,
she's entitled.

00:22:47.104 --> 00:22:49.022
She's getting beat up,
and you keep it from me?

00:22:49.189 --> 00:22:51.691
What if I had told you?
What are you gonna do?

00:22:51.857 --> 00:22:53.692
I don't know, help her.

00:22:53.859 --> 00:22:56.152
How? Go to Chino? See Eddie?

00:22:56.319 --> 00:22:59.612
Land in the hospital or jail or worse?
Theresa was protecting you.

00:22:59.779 --> 00:23:01.864
- You should have told me.
- Well, I didn't.

00:23:02.030 --> 00:23:04.782
Because I knew you'd get
riled up and do something stupid.

00:23:04.949 --> 00:23:06.700
Now that you do know...

00:23:06.867 --> 00:23:09.410
...I sure hope you don't prove me right.

00:23:09.702 --> 00:23:12.162
- What about Theresa?
- She's on her way here.

00:23:12.329 --> 00:23:14.538
If she's around people
that care about her...

00:23:14.705 --> 00:23:16.831
...she's less likely
to go back to him.

00:23:18.457 --> 00:23:22.085
- I gotta get ready for the shower.
- Do we understand each other?

00:23:27.963 --> 00:23:31.340
Hey, is your father around?
I didn't even see him.

00:23:31.507 --> 00:23:33.675
- Then I guess not.
- That's cool. I figured...

00:23:33.842 --> 00:23:36.385
...he'd maybe want to say hey.
Do you know where he is?

00:23:36.594 --> 00:23:38.720
No, didn't say.

00:23:39.721 --> 00:23:42.264
Oh, I know what I wanted to ask you.

00:23:42.472 --> 00:23:44.849
- Did he say anything about the lunch?
- Not really.

00:23:45.057 --> 00:23:48.184
No, I didn't think he would.
I mean, it got a little awkward there...

00:23:48.393 --> 00:23:51.186
...in the comic-book part.
I think it turned a good corner...

00:23:51.395 --> 00:23:53.854
...at, like, the bread basket.
- Bread basket?

00:23:54.021 --> 00:23:56.606
Yeah. Yeah, he asked me,
you know, to pass the bread.

00:23:56.773 --> 00:23:59.983
I said, "You'll wanna go bread stick
as opposed to dinner roll."

00:24:00.150 --> 00:24:02.026
He went bread stick.
Shows he trusts me.

00:24:02.193 --> 00:24:04.153
Didn't clock that.

00:24:05.904 --> 00:24:08.238
So I didn't even get
a review at all, huh?

00:24:08.405 --> 00:24:10.865
Not that I read my own press,
but, I mean...

00:24:11.032 --> 00:24:16.452
...nothing involving thumbs or stars or...
- We should go.

00:24:49.681 --> 00:24:51.807
You should have told me.

00:24:53.767 --> 00:24:55.310
Right.

00:24:55.852 --> 00:24:58.770
Because you would have taken
the news so well.

00:24:59.729 --> 00:25:01.939
You would have tried to kill him.

00:25:02.314 --> 00:25:04.232
He deserves it.

00:25:06.775 --> 00:25:09.110
Yeah, well, this is my problem.

00:25:09.277 --> 00:25:11.153
Not yours.

00:25:11.320 --> 00:25:13.529
I'm the one that has to figure
this thing out.

00:25:13.696 --> 00:25:15.947
What is there to figure out?

00:25:19.158 --> 00:25:21.201
You're not gonna stay with him?

00:25:21.910 --> 00:25:23.410
Right?

00:25:27.955 --> 00:25:30.707
I'll take some self-defense classes.

00:25:31.290 --> 00:25:33.792
And Eddie and I will live
happily ever after.

00:25:33.959 --> 00:25:38.003
- How can you joke?
- Because I'm tired of crying.

00:25:38.378 --> 00:25:40.004
Okay?

00:25:44.090 --> 00:25:46.717
- I haven't seen you like this in a while.
- What?

00:25:46.883 --> 00:25:48.676
Flustered? Upset?

00:25:48.843 --> 00:25:51.595
Heading to a Newport party
against my will?

00:25:51.762 --> 00:25:54.430
Passionate. Driven.

00:25:54.680 --> 00:25:56.723
This is the man I married.

00:25:56.931 --> 00:25:58.557
Oh, yeah?

00:25:58.724 --> 00:26:01.559
So are you ready
to face the happy couple?

00:26:01.726 --> 00:26:04.144
- The gruesome twosome?
- Yeah.

00:26:05.604 --> 00:26:07.104
- Hey.
- Hi.

00:26:07.396 --> 00:26:10.356
So, Theresa, I hope you've decided
to join us for the shower.

00:26:10.857 --> 00:26:13.275
Thanks, but I'm not really
looking my best.

00:26:13.442 --> 00:26:15.193
I have some concealer upstairs...

00:26:15.360 --> 00:26:16.944
...works like a magic wand.

00:26:17.111 --> 00:26:20.196
She's right.
You should see her without the stuff on.

00:26:20.363 --> 00:26:22.114
Terrifying.

00:26:22.614 --> 00:26:25.116
Hey, are you guys ready to go
to the shower?

00:26:27.867 --> 00:26:31.620
- Hey, Theresa.
- Theresa's in town for a while.

00:26:32.871 --> 00:26:35.205
Just till I get things straightened out.

00:26:35.372 --> 00:26:38.666
Of course. Well, then you
should come to the shower.

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:41.751
Thanks.

00:26:52.883 --> 00:26:55.551
- Julie, congratulations.
- Thank you.

00:26:55.718 --> 00:26:59.637
- And, Kirsten, what a lovely party.
- Thank you.

00:27:01.639 --> 00:27:04.057
Is it too early to start drinking?

00:27:04.223 --> 00:27:06.975
I hope not, or I'm in trouble.
Thank you.

00:27:08.101 --> 00:27:12.270
After all your mom's been through,
she deserves a man like Caleb Nichol.

00:27:12.437 --> 00:27:16.731
You two will never have to worry
about money ever again.

00:27:16.898 --> 00:27:18.899
Will you excuse me?

00:27:24.403 --> 00:27:26.821
Which way is the ladies' room?

00:27:28.364 --> 00:27:30.156
Look at her...

00:27:30.323 --> 00:27:33.825
...flirting with her sister's boyfriend
like she's in seventh grade again.

00:27:33.992 --> 00:27:37.369
For once, I actually know what you mean.

00:27:38.870 --> 00:27:42.748
Wonder which of my past humiliations
she's telling him about now.

00:27:43.540 --> 00:27:47.417
Oh, my God.
Did she just say "monster truck"?

00:27:47.584 --> 00:27:49.085
You were into monster trucks?

00:27:49.252 --> 00:27:52.420
I better get over there
or there might not even be a wedding.

00:27:59.508 --> 00:28:01.426
Hey, Juju, your ears must be burning.

00:28:01.634 --> 00:28:05.762
I was telling Cal here about
you and me and Knott's Berry Farm.

00:28:06.429 --> 00:28:09.306
Cindy, thank you
for entertaining Cal here...

00:28:09.473 --> 00:28:11.390
...but you should go. Try the pastries.

00:28:11.724 --> 00:28:14.309
Maybe it'll soak up some of that whiskey.

00:28:15.893 --> 00:28:17.269
Does anybody want anything?

00:28:17.436 --> 00:28:19.646
- Tequila shooter?
- Cindy, go.

00:28:23.315 --> 00:28:25.691
I'm sorry about Cindy.

00:28:25.858 --> 00:28:27.651
She's got oomph. Spark.

00:28:27.817 --> 00:28:29.944
Just like her sister.

00:28:30.110 --> 00:28:32.821
Oh, and Julie looks fabulous.

00:28:32.987 --> 00:28:34.613
Must be all those Yogalates classes.

00:28:34.780 --> 00:28:37.865
Oh, you know,
I've always wanted to try Yogalates.

00:28:38.032 --> 00:28:39.950
- Really?
- Me too. Maybe we should...

00:28:40.117 --> 00:28:42.702
Maybe we'll take a class together,
you and I.

00:28:53.667 --> 00:28:55.168
Needed a break?

00:28:55.668 --> 00:28:57.544
Hey.

00:28:57.836 --> 00:29:00.838
Yeah. I was just feeling
a little lost out there.

00:29:02.589 --> 00:29:04.966
You probably really need Ryan right now.

00:29:05.174 --> 00:29:10.302
- Me being here, I'm getting in the way.
- Hey, it's not your fault.

00:29:10.469 --> 00:29:14.930
Look, part of the reason I didn't want
to tell Ryan about Eddie is because...

00:29:15.097 --> 00:29:17.223
...he seems really happy right now.

00:29:17.765 --> 00:29:19.933
And that's because of you.

00:29:20.225 --> 00:29:22.018
Look, Cal, a juicer.

00:29:22.810 --> 00:29:25.395
- I need one of these.
- How about a game?

00:29:28.314 --> 00:29:29.814
Okay, folks!

00:29:30.482 --> 00:29:35.943
Has anyone here ever played
"How Well Do You Know Them?"

00:29:36.110 --> 00:29:39.237
Cindy, everyone here already knows us.
That won't be much fun.

00:29:39.404 --> 00:29:41.363
All right,
I'm gonna be Chuck Woolery.

00:29:41.530 --> 00:29:43.240
I'm gonna ask a question...

00:29:43.406 --> 00:29:46.325
...and whoever shouts out the most
right answers, wins.

00:29:47.284 --> 00:29:51.703
First question:
What is Julie's favorite meal?

00:29:51.870 --> 00:29:55.164
Oh, I know this. Chilean sea bass
with roasted baby carrots.

00:29:55.330 --> 00:29:57.540
No. No, the answer is:

00:29:57.707 --> 00:30:00.042
Double-Double Cheeseburger,
heavy on the sauce...

00:30:00.208 --> 00:30:03.127
...large fries and an orange soda.
Okay, next question.

00:30:03.335 --> 00:30:06.004
Hi. I've been looking for you.

00:30:06.421 --> 00:30:08.547
For both of you.

00:30:10.798 --> 00:30:13.508
- Everything's okay?
- Yeah, it's just, at a shower.

00:30:13.675 --> 00:30:15.885
Not really what I do.

00:30:20.930 --> 00:30:24.432
- Is that him?
- Yeah, he's just calling to apologize again.

00:30:24.599 --> 00:30:27.184
- I'm not going to get it.
- You been talking to him?

00:30:30.894 --> 00:30:32.729
- Leave her alone.
- What are you doing?

00:30:32.896 --> 00:30:35.355
- What are you doing talking to him?
- Stay out of this.

00:30:35.522 --> 00:30:38.983
Stay out of it? You came here.
You knew I was gonna find out.

00:30:39.149 --> 00:30:42.485
What did you think I was gonna do?
He hit you. You can't go back to him.

00:30:42.652 --> 00:30:44.153
It's not that simple.

00:30:44.319 --> 00:30:46.946
You know him. He's not a bad person.
He made a mistake.

00:30:47.113 --> 00:30:49.072
- You don't really believe that.
- Yes, I do.

00:30:49.239 --> 00:30:51.407
- I know that.
- You're an expert on the subject?

00:30:51.574 --> 00:30:54.159
What are you gonna tell me?
This isn't the first time?

00:30:59.496 --> 00:31:01.455
Has he done it before?

00:31:03.039 --> 00:31:06.166
Tell me, Theresa.
Has he hit you before?

00:31:07.334 --> 00:31:09.127
Ryan.

00:31:12.879 --> 00:31:16.298
Growing up, who was Julie's first love?

00:31:17.048 --> 00:31:18.549
Rick Springfield?

00:31:18.716 --> 00:31:23.761
Close. The entire defensive line
of our eighth-grade football team.

00:31:23.927 --> 00:31:26.679
I refuse to sit here and be humiliated.

00:31:28.889 --> 00:31:30.140
Oh, crap.

00:31:34.142 --> 00:31:37.728
Hey, you're carrying a purse now?
Not that you shouldn't accessorize.

00:31:37.895 --> 00:31:39.229
You stealing Marissa's car?

00:31:39.395 --> 00:31:41.438
If I don't do something,
Theresa's gonna marry that guy.

00:31:41.605 --> 00:31:42.981
- You can't go.
- Yeah, why not?

00:31:43.148 --> 00:31:45.107
It's a horrible idea,
and my dad said not to.

00:31:45.274 --> 00:31:48.776
She's taking his calls. She's gonna
go back to him. It's gonna happen again.

00:31:48.943 --> 00:31:50.652
- Dude, don't.
- I don't have a choice.

00:31:50.819 --> 00:31:54.155
- Hey, man, you do.
- Let go of me. Now.

00:32:00.075 --> 00:32:03.035
- Is Ryan leaving?
- Yeah.

00:32:04.661 --> 00:32:05.995
Oh, he took your car.

00:32:21.338 --> 00:32:23.381
Put down the window.

00:32:25.674 --> 00:32:27.967
- Get out of the car.
- He's done it before.

00:32:28.134 --> 00:32:30.469
- Well, that's the pattern.
- He'll do it again.

00:32:30.636 --> 00:32:34.055
Don't try to fix this thing, kid.
I'm your guardian and I call the shots.

00:32:34.221 --> 00:32:36.431
- Get out of the car.
- Somebody has to stop him.

00:32:36.598 --> 00:32:40.642
Theresa has to decide on her own
to leave Eddie. We can't force her.

00:32:40.851 --> 00:32:44.353
I know about these things.
Theresa, Eddie, Chino.

00:32:44.519 --> 00:32:46.104
- You don't get it.
- Oh, yes, I do.

00:32:46.271 --> 00:32:48.814
I've seen too many kids just like him,
and I know...

00:32:48.981 --> 00:32:51.232
...it will not be you to suddenly
make him change.

00:32:51.399 --> 00:32:53.650
- So you want me to do nothing?
- Yes.

00:32:55.860 --> 00:32:57.653
I can't do that.

00:33:05.824 --> 00:33:07.701
Thank you very much.

00:33:09.952 --> 00:33:13.037
That was quite a scene out there, huh?

00:33:14.371 --> 00:33:16.623
I'll always love Cindy.

00:33:19.583 --> 00:33:23.586
So do you wanna talk about this?

00:33:23.752 --> 00:33:25.837
I know it's weird.

00:33:26.004 --> 00:33:29.548
Even though it was years ago
you and I dated, she's still your sister.

00:33:30.757 --> 00:33:34.759
It's not jealousy. I just don't want to see
my friend make a terrible mistake.

00:33:34.926 --> 00:33:38.762
- What makes you think it's a mistake?
- Jimmy, this is what Hailey does.

00:33:38.928 --> 00:33:40.971
She uses people to get back at me.

00:33:42.931 --> 00:33:44.765
Kirsten...

00:33:46.433 --> 00:33:49.935
...this isn't about you.

00:33:52.062 --> 00:33:55.939
Hailey and I, you know, it feels real.

00:33:57.607 --> 00:33:59.525
Okay.

00:34:00.775 --> 00:34:02.443
It's just that...

00:34:02.610 --> 00:34:04.319
...you're starting to do well...

00:34:04.486 --> 00:34:07.988
...and I don't want to see you...
- Happy? Because that's what I am.

00:34:09.406 --> 00:34:13.158
It's the first time since Julie left me
I don't feel completely alone.

00:34:13.325 --> 00:34:14.951
So...

00:34:15.493 --> 00:34:17.870
...just be happy for me, okay?

00:34:21.080 --> 00:34:22.706
Okay.

00:34:37.048 --> 00:34:38.883
What do you want, Cindy? Money?

00:34:40.258 --> 00:34:43.594
- I don't want your money.
- The hell you don't.

00:34:43.761 --> 00:34:47.430
Why else would you come down here
and humiliate me in front of my friends?

00:34:47.763 --> 00:34:50.640
Those people aren't your friends.
They don't even know you.

00:34:50.807 --> 00:34:53.475
- And you do?
- I used to.

00:34:54.392 --> 00:34:57.978
Back when you had big hair
and you wore tight jeans.

00:34:58.145 --> 00:35:02.272
We were supposed
to leave Riverside together, remember?

00:35:02.439 --> 00:35:07.526
We were gonna move to L.A.
And marry rock stars.

00:35:09.193 --> 00:35:11.278
Then you took off.

00:35:11.862 --> 00:35:13.654
And you moved to the beach...

00:35:13.821 --> 00:35:15.614
...without me.

00:35:17.115 --> 00:35:20.200
I couldn't exactly take you with me.

00:35:23.202 --> 00:35:24.828
I know.

00:35:26.162 --> 00:35:27.580
I just...

00:35:28.247 --> 00:35:31.541
I miss you sometimes, that's all.

00:35:43.006 --> 00:35:46.717
I'm sorry about what happened out there.

00:35:47.092 --> 00:35:49.510
Guess I won't be invited
to the wedding, huh?

00:35:49.677 --> 00:35:51.678
Of course you'll be invited
to the wedding.

00:35:51.845 --> 00:35:54.096
We wouldn't have it any other way.

00:35:54.263 --> 00:35:56.181
Thanks.

00:35:57.182 --> 00:35:58.724
I'll be outside.

00:36:02.518 --> 00:36:05.895
Well, I'm sure you found Cindy's visit
very revealing.

00:36:08.689 --> 00:36:11.982
Julie, there is nothing
I could find out about you...

00:36:12.149 --> 00:36:13.692
...that would make me walk away.

00:36:26.908 --> 00:36:29.827
Hey, you're avoiding me.

00:36:30.494 --> 00:36:32.329
That's cool.
I kind of like it.

00:36:32.495 --> 00:36:35.497
It's kind of a throwback.
It feels very eighth-grade.

00:36:39.041 --> 00:36:43.210
So I'm guessing
that this has something to do...

00:36:44.044 --> 00:36:46.921
...with me bombing with your father.
- It was a train wreck.

00:36:47.088 --> 00:36:49.548
- I was nervous.
- You didn't stop talking.

00:36:49.714 --> 00:36:52.383
I know. I get chatty when I'm...

00:36:52.591 --> 00:36:53.925
...completely terrified.

00:36:54.426 --> 00:36:58.095
Look, next time I'll be...
I'll be the strong silent type.

00:36:58.428 --> 00:37:01.764
Or I'll just be silent, okay?

00:37:02.556 --> 00:37:04.307
Look, my dad and I are best friends.

00:37:04.474 --> 00:37:07.059
We've been through everything together.

00:37:07.684 --> 00:37:10.269
And he's never been wrong.
I mean, he's my dad.

00:37:10.436 --> 00:37:12.979
- And he hated me?
- You just weren't what he expected.

00:37:13.146 --> 00:37:15.522
Yeah? What was he expecting?
Someone taller?

00:37:15.689 --> 00:37:18.774
- Blonder? Presbyterian? What?
- Just different.

00:37:18.983 --> 00:37:20.692
My dad's really protective of me.

00:37:20.859 --> 00:37:25.070
Look, I'm sorry if your dad doesn't think
I'm good enough for you. Really, I am.

00:37:25.278 --> 00:37:28.822
If that's the way he feels, that sucks.
But you know what? It doesn't matter.

00:37:29.031 --> 00:37:33.492
I don't really have to be his type, because
the only thing that matters is me and you.

00:37:33.659 --> 00:37:35.201
Right?

00:37:42.206 --> 00:37:44.457
I have to go.

00:38:03.260 --> 00:38:04.970
I thought you'd be in Chino by now.

00:38:05.262 --> 00:38:07.263
I got as far as Corona.

00:38:07.972 --> 00:38:09.598
And?

00:38:09.931 --> 00:38:13.183
And I realized Eddie wasn't
who I needed to talk to.

00:38:14.601 --> 00:38:18.603
- What are you doing going back to him?
- It won't happen again. He promised.

00:38:18.770 --> 00:38:21.980
- Like he promised the last time, right?
- What am I supposed to do?

00:38:22.147 --> 00:38:24.524
- My whole life is in Chino.
- So was mine.

00:38:24.690 --> 00:38:27.526
Right, so I wait for some rich,
perfect family to adopt me...

00:38:27.692 --> 00:38:30.444
...and stick me
in their beautiful pool house? Great idea.

00:38:30.611 --> 00:38:32.904
- You can stay with the Cohens too.
- No, I can't.

00:38:33.112 --> 00:38:34.613
- Why not?
- Because...

00:38:34.822 --> 00:38:36.781
...I move in there and then what happens?

00:38:36.948 --> 00:38:38.532
I don't know.

00:38:38.949 --> 00:38:40.409
I don't know.

00:38:42.201 --> 00:38:44.661
I know what happens
if you go back to Eddie.

00:38:45.829 --> 00:38:47.538
So do you.

00:38:51.040 --> 00:38:53.375
I am never throwing another party again.

00:38:53.500 --> 00:38:55.210
Oh, honey, don't tease.

00:38:55.376 --> 00:38:58.420
Nothing good happens at our parties.
Have you noticed that?

00:38:59.254 --> 00:39:00.588
Yeah, the gruesome twosome...

00:39:00.755 --> 00:39:04.382
...never tighter.
- Jimmy and Hailey, officially a couple.

00:39:04.549 --> 00:39:07.551
And Ryan's probably heading back
to juvie right about now.

00:39:07.717 --> 00:39:09.051
And if he is...

00:39:09.218 --> 00:39:11.803
...I know just the guy to get him out.

00:39:13.262 --> 00:39:15.514
- Hi.
- Hey, you all right?

00:39:15.931 --> 00:39:17.348
How's Eddie?

00:39:17.515 --> 00:39:20.892
I decided to take my lawyer's advice
and went to see Theresa instead.

00:39:21.518 --> 00:39:23.977
Hi, Mr. Cohen. Mrs. Cohen.

00:39:25.020 --> 00:39:27.313
- You can stay as long as you want.
- Thank you.

00:39:27.521 --> 00:39:29.064
You can sleep in the pool house.

00:39:29.272 --> 00:39:31.816
Ryan, you can bunk in with Seth,
on the air mattress.

00:39:32.024 --> 00:39:34.484
Come on.
Why don't we get you settled in.

00:39:44.324 --> 00:39:45.824
Thanks for doing this.

00:39:46.325 --> 00:39:48.243
Kirsten and I would do anything for you.

00:39:48.535 --> 00:39:50.327
Yeah, me too.

00:39:50.828 --> 00:39:53.079
Well, I'm glad to hear it...

00:39:53.246 --> 00:39:54.830
...because we lost the pump.

00:39:54.997 --> 00:39:57.790
So somebody's gonna have
to blow that sucker up.

00:40:07.380 --> 00:40:10.131
- Hey, Marissa.
- Hey, Kirsten. Is Ryan home?

00:40:10.298 --> 00:40:12.716
Yeah, he's in the pool house.

00:40:12.883 --> 00:40:16.385
He's helping Theresa get settled in.

00:40:16.552 --> 00:40:17.970
So she's staying?

00:40:18.720 --> 00:40:20.304
Yeah.

00:40:21.388 --> 00:40:23.390
He loves you, you know.

00:40:24.098 --> 00:40:28.434
- I know.
- Then make room for her to be in his life.

00:40:28.851 --> 00:40:30.894
He's not going anywhere.

00:40:52.991 --> 00:40:55.576
Sorry I bailed on the shower.

00:40:57.453 --> 00:41:00.830
Don't you think this apology
should be directed elsewhere...

00:41:00.996 --> 00:41:02.581
...like, say, Marissa?

00:41:05.416 --> 00:41:06.959
I guess so.

00:41:09.335 --> 00:41:11.378
I didn't want to, I had to...

00:41:11.545 --> 00:41:14.005
Again, should be directed
somewhere else.

00:41:19.466 --> 00:41:22.552
If it makes you feel any better,
things between me and Summer suck.

00:41:22.718 --> 00:41:25.679
- Because of her dad?
- Of all the love triangles to sink us...

00:41:25.845 --> 00:41:27.847
...it is the least sexy.

00:41:30.515 --> 00:41:33.517
Go talk to your girlfriend.
One of us should be able to.

00:41:34.642 --> 00:41:36.102
Right.

00:42:05.745 --> 00:42:07.580
Hi.

00:42:11.332 --> 00:42:14.876
Today I said I was gonna be there,
and I wasn't.

00:42:16.127 --> 00:42:17.961
It's okay.

00:42:18.962 --> 00:42:21.672
And I know you got a lot
to deal with coming up.

00:42:21.839 --> 00:42:23.840
But we're gonna get through it...

00:42:24.007 --> 00:42:25.466
...together.

00:42:26.216 --> 00:42:27.884
You and me, we're gonna be fine.

00:42:29.885 --> 00:42:31.553
I...

00:42:37.724 --> 00:42:39.183
What?

00:42:41.142 --> 00:42:43.310
I think we are gonna be fine.
